    <!-- ── Donate / about this build (merged into the About page) ────── -->
    <sys:String x:Key="Donate_SupportTitle">Support ScreenSound</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Donate_Desc">ScreenSound is a solo developer project built in spare time. If it's made your multi-monitor setup a little nicer, a one-off tip helps justify the hours spent on bug fixes and new features — the app stays free either way.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Donate_AboutMeTitle">About SimpleScreen</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Donate_AboutMeDesc" xml:space="preserve">This customized build is maintained by xunhualu, built on top of the original ScreenSound:
· Cross-screen sync: window size, colour temperature and brightness stay consistent on every display
· Audio routing locked to its screen, so hidden or minimised windows never drift away
· One-stop monitor control: DDC adjustment, software colour, display rotation
· Multilingual UI: English / Chinese / Japanese / Korean</sys:String>

    <!-- ── Hotkeys ──────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
    <sys:String x:Key="HK_Title">Hotkeys</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="HK_TypingGuard">Each hotkey has two cells — Modifier and Main key — and clicking one only edits that cell. Defaults are Alt+F / Alt+U: modifier combos never conflict with typing. Clearing the modifier cell to a dash makes the bare hotkey step aside while you type. Auto-arrange only touches the secondary display.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="HK_Move_Title">Jump Window to the Other Screen</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="HK_Move_Desc">Focus any window and press the hotkey — it instantly moves to the other display, centred. Maximised windows fill the target screen, minimised ones are restored first. Press again to jump back</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="HK_Key_Title">Hotkey Binding</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="HK_Key_Desc">Set the two cells independently: click the left cell, hold Ctrl / Alt / Shift / Win (any combination) and release to save, or press Backspace to clear it; click the right cell and press a key to set the main key without touching the left cell. The default Alt+F never interferes with typing</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="HK_Record">Record</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="HK_Recording">Press a key (Esc to cancel)…</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="HK_ModifierLabel">Modifier</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="HK_MainKeyLabel">Main key</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="HK_ModifierTip">Click, then hold Ctrl / Alt / Shift / Win (any combination) and release. Backspace clears; Esc cancels</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="HK_KeyBoxTip">Click, then press the key you want to use. Esc cancels</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="HK_ModifierRecording">Hold modifier keys (Ctrl / Alt / Shift / Win, any combination) and release to save; Backspace clears, Esc cancels…</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="HK_KeyRecording">Press the new main key (Esc to cancel)…</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="HK_RegisterFailed">Hotkey registration failed — the combination may already be taken by another program</sys:String>
