    <sys:String x:Key="HK_Switch_Hotkey">Hotkey</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="HK_Switch_Auto">Auto</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="HK_Switch_HotkeyTip">Enables the key-driven tile shortcut. Turning it off leaves auto-optimise untouched.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="HK_Switch_AutoTip">Tiles the secondary screen automatically with no key press. Independent of the hotkey switch.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="HK_Auto_Title">Auto-optimise layout</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="HK_Auto_Desc">No key press needed: when a new window appears on the secondary screen, or a window is shrunk leaving free space, windows are tiled automatically (one fills the screen, two split left/right on a landscape panel or top/bottom on a portrait one, more form a grid). Once tiled the layout is left alone — a custom 30/70 split stays put; it only re-tiles for another new window or clear free space. Only the secondary screen is affected; windows on the primary display are never moved.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="HK_ArrangeKey_Title">Tile layout hotkey</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="HK_ArrangeKey_Desc">Tiles the secondary screen on demand (Alt+U by default), independently of the auto switch. The modifier and main-key cells are edited separately. The primary display is never touched; a bare key yields while typing</sys:String>

